WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.045
Operating near structures increases collision, turbulence, navigation, signal, and visual-occlusion risk.

00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:12.090
Maintain safe standoff, simple escape paths, visual awareness, and conservative speed.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:19.585
Do not enter spaces or fly beneath structures without specific authorization, capability, and procedures.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:29.499
Power lines and energized equipment can be difficult to see and may create serious electrical, electromagnetic, or operational hazards.

00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:35.060
Coordinate with the asset owner and use their required boundaries.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.654
A zoom lens is safer than unnecessary proximity.

00:00:39.654 --> 00:00:47.633
Control exposure to people and vehicles through scheduling, barriers, observers, site escorts, and route design.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:56.580
Stop when unbriefed activity enters the operating area or the crew can no longer maintain required separation.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:03.592
Sensitive sites may restrict imagery, radio use, mapping, cloud processing, storage, or disclosure.

00:01:03.592 --> 00:01:06.251
Confirm requirements before arrival.

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:11.329
Protect credentials, firmware, controllers, networks, media, and inspection systems.

00:01:11.329 --> 00:01:14.472
Collect only scoped asset evidence.

00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:19.067
Avoid unrelated homes, people, security features, or operations.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:24.144
Limit access and retention, and document purpose and authorization.

00:01:24.144 --> 00:01:27.771
Inspection is not permission for surveillance.

00:01:27.771 --> 00:01:41.553
Abort criteria include weather deterioration, signal or navigation uncertainty, aircraft warnings, obstacle conflict, people or vehicles entering the area, privacy concerns, lost communication, or poor data quality.

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:45.664
Safe recovery takes priority over completing coverage.

00:01:45.664 --> 00:01:55.094
At critical sites, coordinate radio use, cybersecurity, photography restrictions, escorts, emergency procedures, and data transfer with the owner.

00:01:55.094 --> 00:02:01.622
Do not assume an aviation approval overrides industrial, security, or process-safety controls.
